   "h2": "3.4 Smoke classification",
   "p": [
    "A sampling period was classified as smoke-affected when an HMS polygon covered the site and the polygon's start–end interval overlapped the sampling window. Over the study sites, HMS polygon intervals clustered in the early morning (roughly 11:00–15:00 UTC, 04:00–08:00 MST) and afternoon (roughly 18:00–24:00 UTC), reflecting the imagery periods analysed rather than the presence or absence of smoke in between. With a strict overlap test, no 09:00–12:00 MST sampling window (16:00–19:00 UTC) was classified as smoke-affected, even on days with smoke polygons over the site both before and after the window. We therefore widened each sampling window by 3 h on either side before testing for overlap, and also recorded whether any polygon covered the site on the relevant HMS days regardless of time. Each period was assigned the highest density class of the overlapping polygons and grouped as none, light or medium–heavy."
   ]
