    "The national sub-daily sites allow the Colorado lag result to be tested where sampling windows differ. Two cautions are needed first. Pooling a lag curve across sites that sample different windows mixes together shifts that mean quite different things — a −3 h shift is the middle of the night for a 05:00 sample and mid-morning for a 12:00 sample — so the pooled curves (Fig. 10) are reported for completeness but are not comparable with Colorado's, where every sample covers the same window. The informative cut is by the hour at which sampling begins (Fig. 11). Second, an 8 h window shifted by 3 h still overlaps the original window by five hours, so lag curves for the 8 h sites are expected to be flat, and they are: the day-to-day correlation is 0.31, 0.38, 0.35 and 0.32 at lags of −3, 0, +3 and +6 h.",
