    "Two caveats belong with that conclusion. The noise estimate is an upper bound on random scan-to-scan error and says nothing about errors that persist through a day, so the ceiling is correspondingly uncertain; and the reported per-cell uncertainties, taken at face value, are larger still and would leave no room for the correlations we observe, which suggests they overstate the random error of the scans they flag as most uncertain. The cloud fraction threshold mattered much less than block size, particularly for all-day means, suggesting that residual cloud contamination is not the dominant error source for daily means, although stricter screening helped when fewer (midday) scans were averaged.",
